        "sourceName": "吴都候选：木渎—胥口考古城址范围（示意）",
        "enName": "Wu capital candidate: Mudu–Xukou archaeological site extent (schematic)",
        "enSourceName": "Wu capital candidate: Mudu–Xukou archaeological site extent (schematic)",
        "label": "木渎—胥口考古城址（约24.8 km²）\n阖闾城位置存在争议",
        "enLabel": "Mudu–Xukou site (c.24.8 km²)\nHelü capital location disputed",
        "referenceUrl": "https://dfzb.suzhou.gov.cn/dfzb/fzxh/201107/2670e6a6682149a0b0777b63d30eecf3.shtml",
        "additionalSourceUrls": [
          "https://www.szlib.com/DR/SuzhouForums/Content/357",
          "https://yangtze.silkroadinfo.org.cn/2017/11/30/20171130110601.pdf"
        ],
        "status": "已确认都邑性城址 · 范围地望示意，非逐边实测墙界",
        "enStatus": "Archaeologically confirmed urban site; schematic geographic extent, not surveyed wall boundaries",
        "labelCoordinates": [
          120.472,
          31.251
        ],
        "reportedAreaKm2": 24.79,
        "areaSourceUrl": "https://www.szlib.com/DR/SuzhouForums/Content/357",
        "wuCapitalCandidate": "archaeological-site",
        "locationPrecision": "据五峰北墙、新峰南墙、穹窿山东麓及刘庄木东路地望概括；连线为示意",
        "note": "重点表达木渎—胥口一带经调查发掘确认的大型都邑性城址。约24.8平方公里取自苏州图书馆张学锋讲座所述24.79平方公里；其他考古介绍常概称24平方公里。现有城墙、壕沟、水门与聚落遗存为考古依据，但本范围不是考古原始GIS、法定保护范围或全圈连续城墙测绘。结合苏州地方志所载五峰北墙、新峰南墙、刘庄木东路东侧及穹窿山东麓西侧地望，以现代OSM地形地名作近似围合；未取得完整可配准的发掘总平面图。四至之间的连接是制图概括，山体可构成天然屏障，不能据闭合线认定每段均有墙体。约24.8是资料记载值，不是按此面积反推的精确墙界；本概括面面积约25.9平方公里。2017年考古学术会议报告指出，尚难与历史吴都直接对应。阖闾城位置存在争议。",
        "enNote": "Emphasizes the archaeologically confirmed large urban site around Mudu and Xukou. The c.24.8 km² figure is the reported 24.79 km² in a Suzhou Library lecture; other archaeological summaries round it to 24 km². The displayed extent is a geographic schematic based on the Wufeng northern remains, Xinfeng southern remains, Liuzhuang/Mudong Road eastern vicinity and eastern foothills of Qionglong, with modern OSM locators. No complete registered excavation plan was obtained. Connecting edges are cartographic generalizations, not surveyed or continuous walls; hills may serve as natural barriers. This schematic polygon is about 25.9 km². Archaeological urban status does not establish identification with Helü’s historical capital; the location is disputed."
      },
